    "headline": "Rubrik pairs fast growth, net cash and strong momentum with a very high valuation, leaving it at Hold.",
    "thesis": "Rubrik scores 57, a Hold, because strong growth, balance sheet and trend scores are offset by a very weak valuation score and middling quality. Revenue was up 37.9% year on year in the latest quarter and up 42.5% on a trailing basis, though growth slowed by 1.1 pp from the previous quarter. The balance sheet holds net cash with cash at 1.54 times debt, and the shares trade 54.7% above their 200-day average and 111.3 pp ahead of SPY over the last 126 trading days. Against that, the stock is expensive in absolute terms at 15.2x sales and 77.2x free cash flow, with an FCF yield 3.9 pp below the 10-year Treasury yield, which gives a valuation score of 4. Quality scores 42: gross margin is 80.2% and FCF margin 19.7%, but the operating margin is -18.3%, stock-based pay is 22.2% of revenue and diluted shares were up 5.8% year on year.",
    "key_risks": [
      "A high absolute valuation (15.2x sales, 77.2x FCF) leaves little room if growth slows further",
      "Operating losses (-18.3% operating margin) and negative EBIT despite positive free cash flow",
      "Heavy stock-based compensation at 22.2% of revenue, with diluted shares up 5.8% year on year",
      "After a sharp run, the shares sit 54.7% above their 200-day average and could pull back",
      "Competition in AI-agent protection, with Cohesity launching a rival product"
